Oracle instrumentation: the eight symbols psx-beetle needed to link.

Apply LAST, after beetle_wtrace_hook / beetle_sio_trace_hook /
beetle_cdcmd_trace_hook / beetle_oracle_buildfix, against beetle-psx
at 5759277b.

docs/beetle-linux.md previously recorded these as unrecoverable ("inventing
semantics", CLAUDE.md rule 14). They are not: every one of them is fully
specified by the consumer already in this repo, so nothing here is a guess.

  beetle_core_get_guest_cycles   runtime/src/beetle_debug_server.c:50 —
      "absolute guest CPU cycles since boot". The core's `timestamp` restarts
      at 0 each retro_run, so absolute = cycles retired by completed frames
      (folded in when Run() returns) + the in-frame timestamp (published by
      the CPU loop once per instruction). Reset on PSX_Power so it counts from
      power-on like the runtime's psx_cycle_count.

  beetle_cyc_watch_{arm,clear,get,get_state}   runtime/src/debug_server.c:2089
      documents the capture semantics the Beetle half "must match EXACTLY",
      including the single-anchor and two-anchor region modes and the
      pc & 0x1FFFFFFF anchor normalisation. Implemented to that spec. Native
      observes at basic-block leaders, Beetle before every instruction — a
      superset, so a block-leader anchor fires at the same architectural point
      on both. The native dedupe of its dispatch+prologue double-fire has no
      Beetle counterpart and is deliberately absent: Beetle cannot double-fire.

  psxrecomp_cdc_irq_type / psxrecomp_dma_int_status
      runtime/src/beetle_libretro.cpp:663-677 spells both out: "CD -> low
      nibble of cdc IRQBuffer (INT type)", "DMA -> DMAIntStatus per-channel
      bitmask".

  retro_psxref_exc_ring_dump   PRECISE_IRQ_SLICE.md:195 lists the fields;
      beetle_debug_server.c:287 says the core emits the complete JSON object,
      forwarded verbatim, and that the comparison is by ORDER + EPC VALUE
      (cross-emulator cycle counts are not comparable). Recorded before
      CP0.SR/CAUSE are rewritten, so `sr` is the state taken FROM.
      NOT recorded: the pending-load slot, which PRECISE_IRQ_SLICE.md lists.
      LDWhich/LDValue are locals of RunReal and the copies in the class are
      stale by the time Exception() runs; reaching them means threading them
      through the signature. Add that if a divergence ever turns on it.

Cost when idle: one int32 store per instruction (the cycle publish) plus a
predicted-not-taken branch on the armed flag. The exception ring records
unconditionally — an exception is rare, and the take-point that matters is
usually the one that happened before anyone thought to arm a trace.

